; ROOFTOP-1 (2026-09-05) - THE EIGHTH SECTION NODE AND ITS VOLUME.
;
; LabRoof is the last two surfaces of Talon's route: the escape hall's ceiling, which is the
; "little tunnel" a player walks across (Route/HallCeil, top y = -16.070), and the void chamber's
; roof they climb onto at the end of it (Route/VoidCeil, top y = -12.206), which is where the
; seventh television stands. x 114..176, z 68..87, anchored at (145, 0, 77.5).
; It exists because the seventh television stands on that roof and
; BubbleTestLayoutTests.EveryTelevisionStandsInsideItsOwnSectionsVolumeInTheShippedScene requires
; every row of TvRoutes to be inside exactly ONE section volume in plan - and its failure message
; is the reason rather than the rule: "a player on that pad is attributed to NO section, so the
; dwell log reports the opposite of the climb they just made." The roof is a place players stand
; and this level had no word for it. See BubbleTestLayout.LabRoofAnchor for why a new section and
; not a wider cyan.
;
; IT IS ADDED LAST, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Bubble ids are the index of an ordinal node-path sort
; over the ADOPTED BUBBLES (BubbleCounter.AdoptAuthoredBubbles). LabRoof carries none, so it
; contributes nothing to that sort and renumbers nothing whatever its position - but adding it
; last means the section order in this file still reads as the order they were added, which is
; what the AllSections doc promises.
[node name="LabRoof" parent="." instance=ExtResource("12_labroof")]
position = Vector3(145, 0, 77.5)

; -17..+70 rather than every other section's -10..+70, because this section's ground is 12-16 m
; UNDER grade: at -10 the television at -12.186 would be below its own section's volume. The floor
; is a BOUNDARY, not a margin - below the tunnel a player walks on (-16.070) and above the floor of
; the black room under it (-17.588), so this box holds everyone on TOP of the lab's escape route
; and nobody inside it. Derived by BubbleTestLayout.VolumeOf and pinned to this file
; number-for-number by TheShippedSceneAuthorsExactlyTheVolumesTheLayoutDerives.
[node name="Volume_LabRoof" type="Area3D" parent="."]
position = Vector3(145, 26.5, 77.5)
script = ExtResource("2_volume")
SectionName = "LabRoof"

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="Volume_LabRoof"]
shape = SubResource("BoxShape3D_labroof")

; LEVEL-4, Talon's note 12 (2026-08-29): "a bunch of golden cubes ... in and around the map ...
; pick them up and throw them with E and Q, this is already created."
;
; NOTHING HERE IS NEW MACHINERY, and that is the point of the note. Crate.tscn is already a
; golden cube -- albedo/emission (0.87, 0.69, 0.13), the tone PropManager's own two slot items
; ship with -- and the NetworkedProp + "Body" idiom below is Playground.tscn's, verbatim
; (scenes/game/world/Playground.tscn, "Props"). PropManager.AdoptAuthoredProps walks the world
; for these, sorts them by node path and hands each a stable id on every peer, so carry, throw
; and the late-join dump work for them exactly as they do for a runtime-spawned prop. No pickup
; class, no interaction, no input binding was written for this.
;
; THEY LIVE IN THIS FILE AND NOT IN A SECTION FILE, deliberately. Carryable._Ready adds an
; outline-shell MeshInstance3D at runtime, and BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckBake fails any SECTION
; whose live node counts exceed its packed ones -- a cube inside a section would turn that check
; red for a reason that is not procedural generation. CheckRootFileHasNoGeometry counts only the
; nodes this file authors ITSELF (recurseIntoInstances: false), so an instanced Crate.tscn adds
; nothing to its tally.
;
; Y IS 0.22 ON THE SURFACE AND -19.78 UNDERGROUND, and both are derived rather than eyeballed:
; the node origin is the cube's centre, Crate.tscn's box is 0.44 m, and every plate's and every
; room floor's top surface is at the section anchor's y. GUARD-1 rays each one and reports the
; gap (BubbleTestSelfTest.CheckPropHeights), which is why these are numbers rather than guesses.

